Substituting the values from Vieta's formulas:\n\\[ r^2 + s^2 + t^2 = 4^2 - 2 \\cdot 5 = 16 - 10 = 6 \\]\n\nTherefore, the length of the long diagonal of the box is:\n\\[ \\sqrt{r^2 + s^2 + t^2} = \\sqrt{6} \\]\n\nThe final answer is:\n\\[ \\boxed{\\sqrt{6}} \\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{\\sqrt{6}}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"intermediate_algebra:67"}
